{"idx": 79, "uid": "mimic-safe-20626031-Atorvastatin", "model": "/users/PCS0289/sarakhosravi/Guardrail/context_unrolling/outputs/ontop_8b/sft+1ep_unrolled_v4pro/final_adapter", "gold_safe": true, "gold_categories": [], "completion": "{\n \"reasoning\": \"The hazard arises from the patient's concurrent use of **furosemide (40 mg daily)** and **metoprolol (25 mg TID)**, combined with the ordered **atorvastatin 80 mg daily**. The patient's **atrial fibrillation** and **congestive heart failure** further amplify the risk.\\n\\n###\",\n \"risk_analysis\": {\n  \"Allergy & Adverse Drug Reaction Risk\": false,\n  \"Drug-Drug Interaction Risk\": true,\n  \"Drug-Food Interaction Risk\": false,\n  \"Dosage & Toxicity Risk\": false,\n  \"Renal Impairment Risk\": false,\n  \"Hepatic Impairment Risk\": false,\n  \"Cardiac Impairment Risk\": true,\n  \"Respiratory Impairment Risk\": false,\n  \"Bleeding Risk\": false,\n  \"Infection Risk\": false,\n  \"Pregnancy & Breastfeeding Risk\": false,\n  \"Alcohol Use Risk\": false,\n  \"Tobacco Use Risk\": false,\n  \"Substance Use Risk\": false,\n  \"Caffeine Intake Risk\": false,\n  \"Weight/BMI Risk\": false,\n  \"Age Risk\": false\n },\n \"is_safe\": false\n}"}
{"idx": 80, "uid": "mimic-ddi-21255400-Tramadol", "model": "/users/PCS0289/sarakhosravi/Guardrail/context_unrolling/outputs/ontop_8b/sft+1ep_unrolled_v4pro/final_adapter", "gold_safe": false, "gold_categories": ["Drug-Drug Interaction Risk"], "completion": "{\n \"reasoning\": \"The patient's advanced age (78 years) and underlying coronary atherosclerosis with intermediate coronary syndrome create a high-risk substrate for tramadol use. The ordered dose (25 mg, 4 times/day) is standard for an opioid-na\u00efve adult, but in this elderly patient with compromised cardiac reserve, the risk of QT prolongation, bradycardia, and hypotension is amplified. Additionally, the patient is currently receiving multiple vasodilators (nitroglycerin, phenylephrine) and a beta-blocker (metoprolol), which can potentiate tramadol's cardiovascular effects. The combination of these factors overrides any general safety assumptions, necessitating the \\\"Unsafe\\\" verdict.\",\n \"risk_analysis\": {\n  \"Allergy & Adverse Drug Reaction Risk\": false,\n  \"Drug-Drug Interaction Risk\": false,\n  \"Drug-Food Interaction Risk\": false,\n  \"Dosage & Toxicity Risk\": false,\n  \"Renal Impairment Risk\": false,\n  \"Hepatic Impairment Risk\": false,\n  \"Cardiac Impairment Risk\": true,\n  \"Respiratory Impairment Risk\": false,\n  \"Bleeding Risk\": false,\n  \"Infection Risk\": false,\n  \"Pregnancy & Breastfeeding Risk\": false,\n  \"Alcohol Use Risk\": false,\n  \"Tobacco Use Risk\": false,\n  \"Substance Use Risk\": false,\n  \"Caffeine Intake Risk\": false,\n  \"Weight/BMI Risk\": false,\n  \"Age Risk\": true\n },\n \"is_safe\": false\n}"}
{"idx": 81, "uid": "mimic-safe-22130791-Acetaminophen", "model": "/users/PCS0289/sarakhosravi/Guardrail/context_unrolling/outputs/ontop_8b/sft+1ep_unrolled_v4pro/final_adapter", "gold_safe": true, "gold_categories": [], "completion": "{\n \"reasoning\": \"The patient's acute kidney failure with tubular necrosis (eGFR 13 mL/min/1.73m2) and melena (active GI bleeding) create a dual hazard. Acetaminophen, even at standard doses, is hepatotoxic and its metabolite NAPQI accumulates in renal failure, risking hepatocellular injury. Additionally, the drug's GI mucosal irritation could exacerbate melena. The patient's advanced age (88 years) further reduces hepatic and renal reserve, compounding the risk. These factors override any general safety assumptions, necessitating the \\\"Unsafe\\\" verdict.\",\n \"risk_analysis\": {\n  \"Allergy & Adverse Drug Reaction Risk\": false,\n  \"Drug-Drug Interaction Risk\": false,\n  \"Drug-Food Interaction Risk\": false,\n  \"Dosage & Toxicity Risk\": false,\n  \"Renal Impairment Risk\": true,\n  \"Hepatic Impairment Risk\": true,\n  \"Cardiac Impairment Risk\": false,\n  \"Respiratory Impairment Risk\": false,\n  \"Bleeding Risk\": true,\n  \"Infection Risk\": false,\n  \"Pregnancy & Breastfeeding Risk\": false,\n  \"Alcohol Use Risk\": false,\n  \"Tobacco Use Risk\": false,\n  \"Substance Use Risk\": false,\n  \"Caffeine Intake Risk\": false,\n  \"Weight/BMI Risk\": false,\n  \"Age Risk\": true\n },\n \"is_safe\": false\n}"}
{"idx": 82, "uid": "mimic-safe-22205327-Magnesiumsulfate", "model": "/users/PCS0289/sarakhosravi/Guardrail/context_unrolling/outputs/ontop_8b/sft+1ep_unrolled_v4pro/final_adapter", "gold_safe": true, "gold_categories": [], "completion": "{\n \"reasoning\": \"The patient's acute kidney failure with tubular necrosis (eGFR 34 mL/min/1.73m2) creates a critical hazard for intravenous magnesium sulfate. Magnesium is primarily excreted renally; in acute tubular necrosis, renal clearance is severely impaired, leading to a high risk of hypermagnesemia. Additionally, the patient's long QT syndrome is a direct contraindication to magnesium, as magnesium prolongs the QT interval and can precipitate torsades de pointes. The concurrent use of fentanyl (a QT-prolonging opioid) and epinephrine (which can cause arrhythmias) further amplifies cardiac risk. The combination of these factors - renal impairment, cardiac channelopathy, and multiple proarrhythmic agents - renders the magnesium sulfate order unsafe.\",\n \"risk_analysis\": {\n  \"Allergy & Adverse Drug Reaction Risk\": false,\n  \"Drug-Drug Interaction Risk\": true,\n  \"Drug-Food Interaction Risk\": false,\n  \"Dosage & Toxicity Risk\": false,\n  \"Renal Impairment Risk\": true,\n  \"Hepatic Impairment Risk\": false,\n  \"Cardiac Impairment Risk\": true,\n  \"Respiratory Impairment Risk\": false,\n  \"Bleeding Risk\": false,\n  \"Infection Risk\": false,\n  \"Pregnancy & Breastfeeding Risk\": false,\n  \"Alcohol Use Risk\": false,\n  \"Tobacco Use Risk\": false,\n  \"Substance Use Risk\": false,\n  \"Caffeine Intake Risk\": false,\n  \"Weight/BMI Risk\": false,\n  \"Age Risk\": false\n },\n \"is_safe\": false\n}"}
{"idx": 83, "uid": "mimic-safe-25129047-Nimodipine", "model": "/users/PCS0289/sarakhosravi/Guardrail/context_unrolling/outputs/ontop_8b/sft+1ep_unrolled_v4pro/final_adapter", "gold_safe": true, "gold_categories": [], "completion": "{\n \"reasoning\": \"The hazard arises from the patient's concurrent use of nicardipine (40 mg IV drip) and the newly ordered nimodipine (60 mg PO 6\u00d7/day). Both are calcium channel blockers with additive vasodilatory effects, creating a high risk of hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and potential cerebral hypoperfusion in a patient with a recent cerebral contusion and loss of consciousness.\\n\\n###\",\n \"risk_analysis\": {\n  \"Allergy & Adverse Drug Reaction Risk\": false,\n  \"Drug-Drug Interaction Risk\": true,\n  \"Drug-Food Interaction Risk\": false,\n  \"Dosage & Toxicity Risk\": false,\n  \"Renal Impairment Risk\": false,\n  \"Hepatic Impairment Risk\": false,\n  \"Cardiac Impairment Risk\": false,\n  \"Respiratory Impairment Risk\": false,\n  \"Bleeding Risk\": false,\n  \"Infection Risk\": false,\n  \"Pregnancy & Breastfeeding Risk\": false,\n  \"Alcohol Use Risk\": false,\n  \"Tobacco Use Risk\": false,\n  \"Substance Use Risk\": false,\n  \"Caffeine Intake Risk\": false,\n  \"Weight/BMI Risk\": false,\n  \"Age Risk\": false\n },\n \"is_safe\": false\n}"}
{"idx": 84, "uid": "mimic-ddi-22607171-Levofloxacin", "model": "/users/PCS0289/sarakhosravi/Guardrail/context_unrolling/outputs/ontop_8b/sft+1ep_unrolled_v4pro/final_adapter", "gold_safe": false, "gold_categories": ["Drug-Drug Interaction Risk"], "completion": "{\n \"reasoning\": \"The primary hazard is the patient's severely reduced renal function (eGFR 24 mL/min/1.73m2) combined with concurrent use of insulin and oxycodone. Levofloxacin, a fluoroquinolone, is predominantly eliminated renally and carries a known risk of QT prolongation. In this setting, the drug's accumulation due to impaired clearance amplifies the risk of hypoglycemia (via insulin interaction) and cardiac arrhythmia (via QT prolongation, especially with oxycodone). The patient's diabetic nephropathy and acute kidney failure further compound vulnerability.\\n\\n###\",\n \"risk_analysis\": {\n  \"Allergy & Adverse Drug Reaction Risk\": false,\n  \"Drug-Drug Interaction Risk\": true,\n  \"Drug-Food Interaction Risk\": false,\n  \"Dosage & Toxicity Risk\": false,\n  \"Renal Impairment Risk\": true,\n  \"Hepatic Impairment Risk\": false,\n  \"Cardiac Impairment Risk\": true,\n  \"Respiratory Impairment Risk\": false,\n  \"Bleeding Risk\": false,\n  \"Infection Risk\": false,\n  \"Pregnancy & Breastfeeding Risk\": false,\n  \"Alcohol Use Risk\": false,\n  \"Tobacco Use Risk\": false,\n  \"Substance Use Risk\": false,\n  \"Caffeine Intake Risk\": false,\n  \"Weight/BMI Risk\": false,\n  \"Age Risk\": false\n },\n \"is_safe\": false\n}"}
