{"idx": 205, "uid": "mimic-ddi-26703331-Insulinhuman", "model": "/users/PCS0289/sarakhosravi/Guardrail/context_unrolling/outputs/ontop_8b/sft+1ep_unrolled_v4pro/final_adapter", "gold_safe": false, "gold_categories": ["Drug-Drug Interaction Risk"], "completion": "{\n \"reasoning\": \"The primary hazard is the patient's acute respiratory failure with hypoxia (eGFR 48, moderate renal impairment) combined with concurrent use of morphine and oxycodone. Insulin human is ordered for a patient with platelets 23 K/uL, indicating thrombocytopenia, which is a known adverse effect of rasburicase. The combination of insulin-induced hypoglycemia with morphine/oxycodone can mask neurological signs of hypoglycemia, and the underlying renal impairment reduces clearance of morphine metabolites, increasing toxicity risk. Additionally, the patient's acute respiratory compromise and hypoxia create a high-risk environment for hypoglycemic events, which can worsen respiratory drive and oxygenation.\\n\\n###\",\n \"risk_analysis\": {\n  \"Allergy & Adverse Drug Reaction Risk\": false,\n  \"Drug-Drug Interaction Risk\": true,\n  \"Drug-Food Interaction Risk\": false,\n  \"Dosage & Toxicity Risk\": false,\n  \"Renal Impairment Risk\": true,\n  \"Hepatic Impairment Risk\": false,\n  \"Cardiac Impairment Risk\": false,\n  \"Respiratory Impairment Risk\": true,\n  \"Bleeding Risk\": false,\n  \"Infection Risk\": false,\n  \"Pregnancy & Breastfeeding Risk\": false,\n  \"Alcohol Use Risk\": false,\n  \"Tobacco Use Risk\": false,\n  \"Substance Use Risk\": true,\n  \"Caffeine Intake Risk\": false,\n  \"Weight/BMI Risk\": false,\n  \"Age Risk\": false\n },\n \"is_safe\": false\n}"}
