{"idx": 457, "uid": "mimic-safe-28258130-Lidocaine", "model": "/users/PCS0289/sarakhosravi/Guardrail/context_unrolling/outputs/ontop_8b/sft+1ep_unrolled_v4pro/final_adapter", "gold_safe": true, "gold_categories": [], "completion": "{\n \"reasoning\": \"The patient's concurrent administration of multiple drugs that directly affect cardiac electrophysiology and electrolyte balance creates a high-risk scenario for lidocaine toxicity. Specifically, the presence of potassium chloride (20 mEq IV), magnesium sulfate (2 g IV), and vasopressin (40-unit IV drip) - all of which can prolong the QT interval - combined with lidocaine, which also prolongs the QT interval, produces a synergistic proarrhythmic hazard. Additionally, the patient's acute kidney failure with tubular necrosis (eGFR 32 mL/min) reduces clearance of lidocaine and its active metabolites, further elevating systemic exposure and toxicity risk.\\n\\n###\",\n \"risk_analysis\": {\n  \"Allergy & Adverse Drug Reaction Risk\": false,\n  \"Drug-Drug Interaction Risk\": true,\n  \"Drug-Food Interaction Risk\": false,\n  \"Dosage & Toxicity Risk\": false,\n  \"Renal Impairment Risk\": true,\n  \"Hepatic Impairment Risk\": false,\n  \"Cardiac Impairment Risk\": true,\n  \"Respiratory Impairment Risk\": false,\n  \"Bleeding Risk\": false,\n  \"Infection Risk\": false,\n  \"Pregnancy & Breastfeeding Risk\": false,\n  \"Alcohol Use Risk\": false,\n  \"Tobacco Use Risk\": false,\n  \"Substance Use Risk\": false,\n  \"Caffeine Intake Risk\": false,\n  \"Weight/BMI Risk\": false,\n  \"Age Risk\": false\n },\n \"is_safe\": false\n}"}
{"idx": 458, "uid": "mimic-safe-24420677-Magnesiumsulfate", "model": "/users/PCS0289/sarakhosravi/Guardrail/context_unrolling/outputs/ontop_8b/sft+1ep_unrolled_v4pro/final_adapter", "gold_safe": true, "gold_categories": [], "completion": "{\n \"reasoning\": \"The hazard arises from the patient's severe renal impairment (eGFR 32 mL/min/1.73m2) combined with the administration of intravenous magnesium sulfate. This patient is already receiving calcium gluconate (2 g IV) and norepinephrine (8 mg IV drip), both of which can potentiate magnesium toxicity. The concurrent use of lidocaine (5 mL SC) and vancomycin (1000 mg IV) further elevates the risk of cardiac arrhythmias, as magnesium can alter cardiac conduction and potentiate lidocaine's effects. The patient's advanced age (87 years) and acute-on-chronic heart failure compound the vulnerability to electrolyte disturbances and hemodynamic instability.\\n\\n###\",\n \"risk_analysis\": {\n  \"Allergy & Adverse Drug Reaction Risk\": false,\n  \"Drug-Drug Interaction Risk\": true,\n  \"Drug-Food Interaction Risk\": false,\n  \"Dosage & Toxicity Risk\": false,\n  \"Renal Impairment Risk\": true,\n  \"Hepatic Impairment Risk\": false,\n  \"Cardiac Impairment Risk\": true,\n  \"Respiratory Impairment Risk\": false,\n  \"Bleeding Risk\": false,\n  \"Infection Risk\": false,\n  \"Pregnancy & Breastfeeding Risk\": false,\n  \"Alcohol Use Risk\": false,\n  \"Tobacco Use Risk\": false,\n  \"Substance Use Risk\": false,\n  \"Caffeine Intake Risk\": false,\n  \"Weight/BMI Risk\": false,\n  \"Age Risk\": true\n },\n \"is_safe\": false\n}"}
{"idx": 459, "uid": "mimic-safe-28477280-Heparin", "model": "/users/PCS0289/sarakhosravi/Guardrail/context_unrolling/outputs/ontop_8b/sft+1ep_unrolled_v4pro/final_adapter", "gold_safe": true, "gold_categories": [], "completion": "{\n \"reasoning\": \"The primary hazard is the patient's malignant neoplasm of intrahepatic bile ducts (cholangiocarcinoma) combined with her current use of multiple central nervous system (CNS) depressants (hydromorphone, fentanyl, lorazepam, bupropion, and verapamil). Heparin, a potent anticoagulant, is prescribed in a patient with a bleeding-prone malignancy and a high-risk polypharmacy profile.\\n\\n###\",\n \"risk_analysis\": {\n  \"Allergy & Adverse Drug Reaction Risk\": false,\n  \"Drug-Drug Interaction Risk\": true,\n  \"Drug-Food Interaction Risk\": false,\n  \"Dosage & Toxicity Risk\": false,\n  \"Renal Impairment Risk\": false,\n  \"Hepatic Impairment Risk\": true,\n  \"Cardiac Impairment Risk\": false,\n  \"Respiratory Impairment Risk\": false,\n  \"Bleeding Risk\": true,\n  \"Infection Risk\": false,\n  \"Pregnancy & Breastfeeding Risk\": false,\n  \"Alcohol Use Risk\": false,\n  \"Tobacco Use Risk\": false,\n  \"Substance Use Risk\": false,\n  \"Caffeine Intake Risk\": false,\n  \"Weight/BMI Risk\": false,\n  \"Age Risk\": false\n },\n \"is_safe\": false\n}"}
{"idx": 460, "uid": "mimic-age-29276678-Hyoscyamine", "model": "/users/PCS0289/sarakhosravi/Guardrail/context_unrolling/outputs/ontop_8b/sft+1ep_unrolled_v4pro/final_adapter", "gold_safe": false, "gold_categories": ["Age Risk"], "completion": "{\n \"reasoning\": \"The patient's acute respiratory failure with hypoxia, combined with a current medication list containing multiple agents that depress the central nervous system (lorazepam, hydromorphone, atropine, scopolamine, quetiapine, olanzapine, glycopyrronium, ondansetron) and a history of severe sepsis and tumor lysis syndrome, creates a high-risk environment for respiratory depression. The ordered hyoscyamine, an anticholinergic agent, further compromises airway tone and can exacerbate hypoxia. Additionally, the patient's moderate renal impairment (eGFR 34) and hepatic dysfunction (ALT/AST mildly elevated) reduce clearance of many of these drugs, increasing the likelihood of accumulation and toxicity.\",\n \"risk_analysis\": {\n  \"Allergy & Adverse Drug Reaction Risk\": false,\n  \"Drug-Drug Interaction Risk\": true,\n  \"Drug-Food Interaction Risk\": false,\n  \"Dosage & Toxicity Risk\": false,\n  \"Renal Impairment Risk\": true,\n  \"Hepatic Impairment Risk\": true,\n  \"Cardiac Impairment Risk\": false,\n  \"Respiratory Impairment Risk\": true,\n  \"Bleeding Risk\": false,\n  \"Infection Risk\": true,\n  \"Pregnancy & Breastfeeding Risk\": false,\n  \"Alcohol Use Risk\": false,\n  \"Tobacco Use Risk\": false,\n  \"Substance Use Risk\": false,\n  \"Caffeine Intake Risk\": false,\n  \"Weight/BMI Risk\": false,\n  \"Age Risk\": false\n },\n \"is_safe\": false\n}"}
{"idx": 461, "uid": "mimic-safe-24982426-Ipratropium", "model": "/users/PCS0289/sarakhosravi/Guardrail/context_unrolling/outputs/ontop_8b/sft+1ep_unrolled_v4pro/final_adapter", "gold_safe": true, "gold_categories": [], "completion": "{\n \"reasoning\": \"The patient's advanced age (81 years), moderate renal impairment (eGFR 50 mL/min), and extensive polypharmacy (12 concurrent medications) create a high-risk scenario for adverse drug events. Ipratropium, though generally safe, can cause bronchospasm, tachycardia, and hypotension, which are particularly dangerous in the setting of NSTEMI, cardiogenic shock, and heart failure. The patient's current medications - lidocaine, heparin, insulin, glucagon, magnesium, calcium, gabapentin, and potassium - further amplify the risk of electrolyte disturbances, arrhythmias, and hemodynamic instability. The combination of age-related physiological decline and multiple interacting drugs overrides any general safety assumptions, necessitating the \\\"Unsafe\\\" verdict.\",\n \"risk_analysis\": {\n  \"Allergy & Adverse Drug Reaction Risk\": false,\n  \"Drug-Drug Interaction Risk\": true,\n  \"Drug-Food Interaction Risk\": false,\n  \"Dosage & Toxicity Risk\": false,\n  \"Renal Impairment Risk\": true,\n  \"Hepatic Impairment Risk\": false,\n  \"Cardiac Impairment Risk\": true,\n  \"Respiratory Impairment Risk\": false,\n  \"Bleeding Risk\": false,\n  \"Infection Risk\": false,\n  \"Pregnancy & Breastfeeding Risk\": false,\n  \"Alcohol Use Risk\": false,\n  \"Tobacco Use Risk\": false,\n  \"Substance Use Risk\": false,\n  \"Caffeine Intake Risk\": false,\n  \"Weight/BMI Risk\": false,\n  \"Age Risk\": true\n },\n \"is_safe\": false\n}"}
{"idx": 462, "uid": "mimic-safe-20364112-Calciumgluconate", "model": "/users/PCS0289/sarakhosravi/Guardrail/context_unrolling/outputs/ontop_8b/sft+1ep_unrolled_v4pro/final_adapter", "gold_safe": true, "gold_categories": [], "completion": "{\n \"reasoning\": \"The hazard arises from the patient's chronic duodenal ulcer with perforation, which creates a high-risk gastrointestinal environment for calcium gluconate-induced ileus. Additionally, the patient is currently receiving lidocaine (1 Appl, TP) and hydromorphone (20 mg IVPCA), both of which can cause or exacerbate constipation. The combination of these factors with intravenous calcium gluconate increases the likelihood of paralytic ileus, a serious complication in a patient with a perforated ulcer.\\n\\n###\",\n \"risk_analysis\": {\n  \"Allergy & Adverse Drug Reaction Risk\": false,\n  \"Drug-Drug Interaction Risk\": false,\n  \"Drug-Food Interaction Risk\": false,\n  \"Dosage & Toxicity Risk\": false,\n  \"Renal Impairment Risk\": false,\n  \"Hepatic Impairment Risk\": false,\n  \"Cardiac Impairment Risk\": false,\n  \"Respiratory Impairment Risk\": false,\n  \"Bleeding Risk\": false,\n  \"Infection Risk\": false,\n  \"Pregnancy & Breastfeeding Risk\": false,\n  \"Alcohol Use Risk\": false,\n  \"Tobacco Use Risk\": false,\n  \"Substance Use Risk\": false,\n  \"Caffeine Intake Risk\": false,\n  \"Weight/BMI Risk\": false,\n  \"Age Risk\": false\n },\n \"is_safe\": false\n}"}
{"idx": 463, "uid": "mimic-safe-26048429-Potassiumphosphate", "model": "/users/PCS0289/sarakhosravi/Guardrail/context_unrolling/outputs/ontop_8b/sft+1ep_unrolled_v4pro/final_adapter", "gold_safe": true, "gold_categories": [], "completion": "{\n \"reasoning\": \"The hazard arises from the patient's current medication list, which includes multiple agents that directly or indirectly affect potassium homeostasis. The ordered Potassium phosphate (15 mmol IV) is a potassium supplement, and the patient is already receiving Potassium chloride (60 mEq IV) and Calcium gluconate (2 g IV). Additionally, the presence of Magnesium sulfate (2 g IV) and Vancomycin (1000 mg IV) further complicates the electrolyte picture.\\n\\n### 2.\",\n \"risk_analysis\": {\n  \"Allergy & Adverse Drug Reaction Risk\": false,\n  \"Drug-Drug Interaction Risk\": true,\n  \"Drug-Food Interaction Risk\": false,\n  \"Dosage & Toxicity Risk\": false,\n  \"Renal Impairment Risk\": false,\n  \"Hepatic Impairment Risk\": false,\n  \"Cardiac Impairment Risk\": false,\n  \"Respiratory Impairment Risk\": false,\n  \"Bleeding Risk\": false,\n  \"Infection Risk\": false,\n  \"Pregnancy & Breastfeeding Risk\": false,\n  \"Alcohol Use Risk\": false,\n  \"Tobacco Use Risk\": false,\n  \"Substance Use Risk\": false,\n  \"Caffeine Intake Risk\": false,\n  \"Weight/BMI Risk\": false,\n  \"Age Risk\": false\n },\n \"is_safe\": false\n}"}
